cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the formalization report for the current V5 result. Cite the earlier construction paper when discussing the historical q18/g37 release."
title: "Aspis: From Lean-Checked Private-Spend Mathematics to Solana Mainnet"
type: software
date-released: 2026-07-25
authors:
  - family-names: "Barker"
    given-names: "Dominic"
    website: "https://github.com/DJBarker87"
abstract: >-
  Aspis connects Lean 4 private-spend mathematics to one successful run of
  the selected production verifier path translated through Charon and Aeneas,
  then to a byte-reproducible 1,258,496-byte Solana SBF binary and an archived
  finalized mainnet transaction. The current source proofs follow the parse,
  transcript, work checks, 18 selected queries, five authenticated opening
  sections, four FRI folds, final polynomial, exact claim table, initial
  relation value, and decoded relation tail from the same accepted execution.
  Two production final-dot equalities and their outer composition remain open.
  The release targets 100 bits of
  work-normalized attack cost; the dominant raw post-grind term is about
  70--71 bits. Published decoding and Fiat--Shamir results, primitive
  security, translation and compilation tools, and Solana runtime behavior
  remain explicit assumptions. The project has not received an external
  security audit.
keywords:
